{"title":"Economic inequality does not equate to poor well-being or mental health","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/939567530/0/marginalrevolution~Economic-inequality-does-not-equate-to-poor-wellbeing-or-mental-health.html","date":1767339979000,"content":"<blockquote><p>A meta-analysis of 168 studies covering more than 11 million people found no reliable link between economic inequality and well-being or mental health. In other words, living in a place that has large gaps between the rich and poor does not affect these outcomes, with implications for policy.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-025-03833-8?utm_source=x&amp;utm_medium=social&amp;utm_campaign=nature&amp;linkId=31730782\" target=\"_blank\">the Nature link</a>, this claim has been bad science all along.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/01/economic-inequality-does-not-equate-to-poor-well-being-or-mental-health.html\">Economic inequality does not equate to poor well-being or mental health</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/939567530/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/939567530/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/939567530/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/939567530/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/939567530/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://